{"title":"Life Sciences Teacher / Lecturer Roadmap","role":"Life Sciences Teacher / Lecturer","summary":"A Life Sciences Teacher/Lecturer teaches biological sciences across school, undergraduate and higher-education settings. The career can cover cell biology, genetics, microbiology, biochemistry, ecology, physiology, biotechnology and related life-science disciplines.","facts":{"Current degree":"B.Sc. — Life Sciences / Biological Sciences","Timeline assumption":"Four-year B.Sc. route beginning in 2026 and graduating around 2030. If the programme is three years, compress the roadmap accordingly."},"about":[{"label":"Career-route check","text":"This is a strong academic alignment, but the requirements differ substantially between school teaching and college/university lecturing. A B.Sc. alone is generally not sufficient for every formal teaching/lecturer position. School teaching may require a recognised teacher-education qualification and applicable eligibility tests, while higher-education teaching normally requires relevant postgraduate study and applicable eligibility/recruitment requirements."}],"intro":[{"type":"table","header":["Item","Roadmap"],"rows":[[{"text":"Starts"},{"text":"Year 1 UG · 2026"}],[{"text":"Degree"},{"text":"B.Sc."}],[{"text":"Course"},{"text":"Life Sciences / Biological Sciences"}],[{"text":"Target career"},{"text":"Teacher / Lecturer"}],[{"text":"Primary domains"},{"text":"Biology, life sciences, education and research"}],[{"text":"Core subjects"},{"text":"Cell biology, genetics, microbiology, biochemistry, physiology, ecology, evolution"}],[{"text":"School route"},{"text":"B.Sc. → recognised teacher-education qualification → applicable eligibility/recruitment"}],[{"text":"Higher-education route"},{"text":"B.Sc. → M.Sc./relevant PG → applicable eligibility/research route → Lecturer/Faculty"}],[{"text":"Long-term roles"},{"text":"Senior Teacher → Subject Lead / Faculty → Academic Coordinator / Professor / Academic Leader"}]]}],"horizons":[